      "coefficients": [
        1.0,
        0.03,
        0.3,
        0.007
      ],
      "rationale": "Weighted neighbor-edge density captures which substantial alternatives conflict with each other, using exact edge products normalized by squared neighbor mass. Resource-boundary destruction pairs this witness with generic gap-normalized reward; no contact IDs or particular gap values enter coefficients. Dynamic ranking constructs the patch before the shared improving swaps, with modest feature allowance and online mutation."
    },
